# GLON-CAR at CRVAL2 = -30 with an explicit LONPOLE = 0 (synthetic,
# hand-written). For theta_0 = 0 the reference point (phi_0, 0) = (0, 0)
# with phi_p = LONPOLE = 0 needs cos(delta_p) = sin(delta_0) < 0: there is
# no native pole, so wcslib refuses the header. Its default would be
# LONPOLE = 180 (delta_0 < theta_0), which is valid: a reader that treats an
# explicit LONPOLE = 0 as "unset" silently substitutes it and returns
# coordinates. For CAR/AIT (theta_0 = 0) an explicit LONPOLE = 0 is either
# the default (delta_0 >= 0: the real sample_msx_*/sample_rosat_* survey
# headers, CRVAL2 = 0) or invalid like this, so this refusal is what pins
# the rule on GLON-CAR; lonpole_tan_dec40_lp0 pins it on a header that
# wcslib accepts.
# EXPECT-WCSLIB-ERROR: Ill-conditioned coordinate transformation parameter
NOTE reject: lonpole_glon_car_bm30_lp0
GRID 1 512 9 1 512 9
PIX 256.5 256.5
SKYGRID 70 130 7 -55 -5 6
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 512
NAXIS2  = 512
CTYPE1  = 'GLON-CAR'
CTYPE2  = 'GLAT-CAR'
CRVAL1  = 100.0
CRVAL2  = -30.0
CRPIX1  = 256.5
CRPIX2  = 256.5
CDELT1  = -0.1
CDELT2  = 0.1
LONPOLE = 0.0
